  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.824pt, 399.72pt, "Abstract: ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(127.73pt, 399.72pt, "The transient response of surface acoustic wave sensors is important for ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 420.36pt, "understanding their dynamic behavior, propagation delay, and response to time-varying signals. ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 441pt, "In this work, the time-domain propagation characteristics of a magnetoelectric SAW sensor ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 461.66pt, "based on a multilayer Love-wave delay line are investigated using complementary numerical ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 482.54pt, "and experimental approaches. Time-domain analysis is employed to determine the delay time ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 503.18pt, "and to extract the phase and group velocities, while frequency-domain analysis provides an ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 523.82pt, "independent characterization of the wave dispersion. Both numerically and experimentally, the ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 544.49pt, "phase and group velocities are found to differ, reflecting the dispersion of the Love wave in the ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 565.37pt, "multilayer structure. At the operating frequency of 146 MHz, the simulated group velocity ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 586.01pt, "obtained from wave-field tracking agrees within 0.4% with the value determined from the ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 606.65pt, "frequency-domain dispersion relation. The simulated delay time and group velocity also show ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 627.31pt, "good agreement with experiment, with deviations of 2.7% in delay time and 0.9% in group ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 648.19pt, "velocity. These results demonstrate the consistency of the time- and frequency-domain analyses ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 668.83pt, "and provide a quantitative characterization of the transient propagation behavior of SAW ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 689.47pt, "sensors. ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 710.14pt, "Keywords: Magnetoelectric sensors, Piezoelectric effect, Surface acoustic waves, Time-domain ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 730.78pt, "analysis ")
]

// arXiv source page 2
#original-page(595.2pt, 841.92pt, none)[
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.824pt, 82.1pt, "1. Introduction ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.824pt, 102.74pt, "Precise measurement of magnetic fields is crucial for a wide range of applications, including ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 123.65pt, "medical diagnostics and industrial monitoring [1–9]. Among various sensing technologies, ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 144.29pt, "surface acoustic wave (SAW) sensors are widely used because of their high sensitivity and ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 164.93pt, "capability to detect minute magnetic field variations over a broad frequency range [10–16]. ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 185.57pt, "These sensors typically rely on the Δ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(272.04pt, 185.57pt, "E")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(279.24pt, 185.57pt, " effect, whereby the mechanical stiffness of a ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 206.47pt, "magnetostrictive layer changes in response to an external magnetic field [17–20]. This variation ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 227.11pt, "in material properties modulates the velocity of the propagating SAW, which can be detected ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 247.75pt, "as a phase shift at the output. The influence of magnetic-field-dependent material properties on ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 268.39pt, "propagation characteristics has been investigated in SAW devices [21–24]. ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 289.3pt, "SAW sensors commonly utilize a piezoelectric substrate such as ST-cut quartz or a piezoelectric ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 309.94pt, "thin film, such as aluminium scandium nitride (AlScN) thin films, to generate and detect ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 330.58pt, "acoustic waves via interdigital transducers (IDTs) [11,15]. A guiding layer is often deposited ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 351.22pt, "on the piezoelectric material to confine the acoustic energy near the surface, thereby enhancing ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 372.12pt, "the interaction between the SAW and the magnetostrictive layer. Recent studies have explored ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 392.76pt, "various approaches to enhance the sensitivity of SAW magnetic field sensors, such as exploiting ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 413.4pt, "the slow-wave phenomenon in phononic crystals (PnCs) [25,26] or strong magnon–phonon ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 434.04pt, "coupling in acoustic cavities [27]. ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 454.94pt, "Several analytical and numerical approaches have been employed to describe the propagation ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 475.58pt, "characteristics of SAW delay-line devices [28]. In particular, the finite element method (FEM) ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 496.22pt, "has been widely used to model Love-wave delay-line devices [14,29–31]. Time-domain ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 516.86pt, "analysis ")
  #line-at(123.132pt, 516.86pt, "provides ")
  #line-at(178.308pt, 516.86pt, "information ")
  #line-at(249.072pt, 516.86pt, "complementary ")
  #line-at(337.596pt, 516.86pt, "to ")
  #line-at(360.864pt, 516.86pt, "conventional ")
  #line-at(436.44pt, 516.86pt, "frequency-domain ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 537.77pt, "characterization of SAW sensors. While frequency-domain analysis is well suited to ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 558.41pt, "determining resonance and dispersion characteristics, time-domain simulation provides access ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 579.05pt, "to the spatiotemporal evolution of the acoustic field, allowing wave propagation to be examined ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 599.69pt, "through the motion of wave peaks and wavefronts. This is particularly relevant for multilayer ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 620.59pt, "Love-wave structures, where the spatial distribution of acoustic energy influences the ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 641.23pt, "relationship between phase and group velocities. The temporal evolution of the output signal ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 661.87pt, "also provides a measure of the propagation delay through the delay line, which is related to the ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 682.51pt, "group velocity. The delay time further determines the temporal averaging inherent to a delay-")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 703.18pt, "line sensor and consequently influences its response to time-varying input signals [32]. Thus, ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 724.06pt, "time-domain analysis provides a framework for relating the propagation characteristics of the ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 744.696pt, "SAW to the dynamic response of the sensor. ")
]

