#original-page(595.2pt, 841.92pt, (image("graphics/page-03.png", width: 15.5pt), 306.5pt, 414.5pt))[
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.824pt, 82.1pt, "In this work, we present a systematic time-domain analysis of a magnetoelectric SAW sensor ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 102.74pt, "based on a multilayer Love-wave delay-line configuration. The present study focuses on the ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 123.65pt, "propagation characteristics and transient response of the sensor rather than its magnetic sensing ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 144.29pt, "performance. A 3D FEM model is developed to simulate the transient response to sinusoidal ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 164.93pt, "electrical excitation and to directly extract the delay time, phase velocity, and group velocity ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 185.57pt, "from the simulated time-dependent wave field. While FEM models have previously combined ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 206.47pt, "frequency- and time-domain analyses [31] to determine the phase velocity and coupling ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 227.11pt, "coefficient of non-dispersive SAWs, we extract both velocities directly from the transient wave ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 247.75pt, "field of a layered, dispersive Love-wave delay line. The results are compared with those ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 268.39pt, "obtained from frequency-domain simulations and further validated experimentally. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
