  #line-at(70.824pt, 436.92pt, "This work presented a systematic investigation of the transient propagation characteristics of a ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 457.82pt, "magnetoelectric SAW sensor based on a multilayer Love-wave delay line using complementary ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 478.46pt, "time- and frequency-domain analyses. The propagation delay, phase velocity, and group ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 499.1pt, "velocity were directly extracted from the transient response within a 3D FEM framework, with ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 519.74pt, "the results cross-validated against independent frequency-domain dispersion analysis and ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 540.65pt, "experimental measurements. At the operating frequency of 146 MHz, a phase velocity of ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 561.29pt, "4271 m/s and a group velocity of 3419 m/s were obtained. The difference between these two ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 581.93pt, "velocities demonstrates the dispersive nature of the Love wave and is consistent with the ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 602.57pt, "dispersion characteristics obtained independently from the frequency-domain analysis, where a ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 623.47pt, "phase velocity of 4105 m/s and a group velocity of 3405 m/s were calculated. ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 644.11pt, "The simulated delay time at 146 MHz was 1.321 μs, compared with 1.357 μs measured ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 664.75pt, "experimentally, corresponding to a deviation of 2.7%. The group velocity obtained from ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 685.39pt, "wavefront tracking also showed good agreement with the experimental value, with a deviation ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 706.3pt, "of approximately 0.9%. These results demonstrate the consistency of the time-domain approach ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 726.94pt, "with the frequency-domain analysis and experimental measurements, confirming the accuracy ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 747.576pt, "of the numerical model in reproducing the experimentally observed transient response. ")
]

