  #line-at(183.19pt, 82.1pt, "Spectrum Instrumentation")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(309.96pt, 82.1pt, ". The M4i.4451-x8 is utilized as the clock ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 102.74pt, "source. It is noteworthy that both cards operate on a shared clock, facilitating synchronized ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 123.65pt, "signal generation and recording at a rate of 500 MS/s. The generated signal has a power of ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 144.29pt, "0 dBm. The recording process is initiated automatically upon the detection of a signal level of ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 164.93pt, "50 mV on the reference channel, and the recording covers 256 pre-trigger data points. The ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 185.57pt, "sensor under investigation is placed in a magnetically shielded environment throughout the ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 206.47pt, "entire measurement. ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 227.11pt, "The recorded measurement signal is first up-sampled by a factor of 10 using cubic spline ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 247.75pt, "interpolation. This is possible because the frequencies under investigation are lower than the ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 268.39pt, "Nyquist frequency (250 MHz) of the data acquisition system. This up-sampling process ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 289.3pt, "improves the temporal resolution to 200 ps. The initial signal generation recorded on the ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 309.94pt, "reference channel defines ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(195.91pt, 309.94pt, "t")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(199.3pt, 309.94pt, "=0 s. Furthermore, the recorded measurement signal is corrected for ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 330.58pt, "the influence of the cables used (2×3 m CLF100) in terms of both its delay and amplitude. All ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 351.22pt, "measurements were performed in a magnetic shield with no applied bias field. This approach ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 372.12pt, "was justified by the fact that the SAW velocity under zero-field conditions is equivalent to that ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 392.76pt, "under magnetic saturation. This simplifies the measurement setup and reduces external noise ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 413.4pt, "sources. ")
